1
00:00:05,464 --> 00:00:08,007
Thanks to Kayoko,
we're working around the clock.

2
00:00:08,132 --> 00:00:11,053
I heard the Faceless nabbed
another bender last night.

3
00:00:13,430 --> 00:00:14,347
<i>Shame.</i>

4
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:15,640
The Brigade just sees you

5
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:17,266
as muscle, sister.

6
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:18,936
What a waste.

7
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:20,646
No!

8
00:00:20,771 --> 00:00:22,272
Uki!

9
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:23,607
We have to go save her.

10
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,735
<i>I don't understand the Anomaly.</i>

11
00:00:27,736 --> 00:00:29,613
<i>It hurts other people, but...</i>

12
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:33,116
<i>it shows us memories
of our Mom and Dad.</i>

13
00:00:33,617 --> 00:00:36,203
We have to find out
what happened to us.

14
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:47,421
No sign of even
a single Haven Envoy.

15
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:48,631
It's been weeks!

16
00:00:48,632 --> 00:00:50,092
A trek across the Harshlands

17
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:51,384
is never easy.

18
00:00:51,385 --> 00:00:53,010
Any minute,
we'll be hearing trumpets

19
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,221
for their arrival.

20
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:56,931
Ever the optimist.

21
00:00:56,932 --> 00:00:59,601
Or the fool. Time will tell.

22
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:02,729
And if you're wrong,

23
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:04,690
what will happen to our home?

24
00:01:04,815 --> 00:01:07,484
We don't need to answer
that question just yet.

25
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:15,826
<i>Fire.</i>

26
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:17,452
<i>Air.</i>

27
00:01:17,578 --> 00:01:18,870
<i>Water.</i>

28
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:20,581
<i>Earth.</i>

29
00:01:21,582 --> 00:01:25,960
<i>Long ago, the Avatar,
master of all four elements,</i>

30
00:01:25,961 --> 00:01:28,337
<i>brought forth the Cataclysm.</i>

31
00:01:28,338 --> 00:01:29,964
<i>Out of the devastation,</i>

32
00:01:29,965 --> 00:01:32,925
<i>the world built
The Seven Havens.</i>

33
00:01:32,926 --> 00:01:35,011
<i>Now the Avatar has returned,</i>

34
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:38,389
<i>but for the first time,
there are two.</i>

35
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:40,309
<i>Most fear they'll destroy
the world again,</i>

36
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:43,937
<i>but I believe
they will save it.</i>

37
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:52,863
Hmm?

38
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:55,449
Why isn't it working?

39
00:01:55,574 --> 00:01:58,035
Meditation can't be rushed.

40
00:02:00,996 --> 00:02:03,748
How exactly will this make us
stronger Avatars?

41
00:02:03,749 --> 00:02:05,292
Being the Avatar isn't only

42
00:02:05,417 --> 00:02:07,502
about being a great bender,
Nisha.

43
00:02:09,211 --> 00:02:12,174
The Avatar is the bridge
between our world

44
00:02:12,299 --> 00:02:13,841
and the spirit world.

45
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:16,886
Centering your spiritual core
is an important part

46
00:02:16,887 --> 00:02:18,221
of your training.

47
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,226
You need to clear your mind.

48
00:02:24,186 --> 00:02:25,728
Take a deep breath in.

49
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:35,697
Dry hay?! My nose nemesis!

50
00:02:36,365 --> 00:02:38,450
If you don't take
this seriously,

51
00:02:38,575 --> 00:02:40,826
you'll never strengthen
your Avatar skills

52
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:43,704
and unlock the memories
you're searching for!

53
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:44,831
Meh.

54
00:02:45,374 --> 00:02:47,083
Ooh! New plan!

55
00:02:47,084 --> 00:02:48,919
I'm going to get
some singing bowls

56
00:02:49,044 --> 00:02:50,212
from Shilpa!

57
00:02:50,337 --> 00:02:51,462
That'll help center you!

58
00:02:51,463 --> 00:02:53,589
Good! I'm starving!

59
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:56,300
Uh... Not that kind of bowl.

60
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:01,013
Wanna build a fort?

61
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,517
We could make
Ruhi's Towering Inferno

62
00:03:03,642 --> 00:03:04,934
of Wind and Sand!

63
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:06,936
Or Geet's Fortress of Mud!

64
00:03:06,937 --> 00:03:09,480
Those memories are somewhere
in our heads.

65
00:03:09,481 --> 00:03:12,817
We've already tried everything!

66
00:03:12,818 --> 00:03:14,319
Now, about this Fortress of Mud.

67
00:03:14,444 --> 00:03:15,695
I've been thinking...

68
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:18,280
there's one thing
we haven't tried:

69
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:20,200
connecting
with the Anomaly again.

70
00:03:21,868 --> 00:03:24,830
Sure! Let's just zap ourselves
for fun.

71
00:03:24,955 --> 00:03:26,372
Great idea!

72
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:29,250
Uh, I think you've been standing
on your head too long.

73
00:03:29,251 --> 00:03:31,961
We survived it! Twice!

74
00:03:31,962 --> 00:03:33,839
There's still a bunch
of Anomaly crystals

75
00:03:33,964 --> 00:03:35,048
at the hospital.

76
00:03:35,173 --> 00:03:38,134
If we touch one,
maybe we'll see our parents!

77
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:39,468
Mmm...

78
00:03:39,469 --> 00:03:41,804
There's a chance we'd be able
to learn more

79
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:43,056
about the Anomaly,

80
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:45,558
do some heroic Avatar stuff.

81
00:03:45,559 --> 00:03:47,977
I do like heroic Avatar stuff.

82
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:49,646
Mm-mm.

83
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:59,822
Oh, so that's how they sing.

84
00:03:59,823 --> 00:04:02,283
Come on, Jae,
we're going Anomaly hunting!

85
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:05,911
You said we needed a new plan,
so this is really your fault!

86
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:27,350
Pavi, I don't know about this.

87
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:34,524
Pavi! Stop!

88
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,573
Okay.

89
00:04:42,574 --> 00:04:44,700
Let's all take a big step back

90
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,619
from the scary
dangerous crystals.

91
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,996
What was it? What did you see?

92
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:50,664
It was so fast.

93
00:04:50,665 --> 00:04:52,458
But I felt...

94
00:04:52,459 --> 00:04:53,710
...broken?

95
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:02,511
That is definitely
not up to code.

96
00:05:07,641 --> 00:05:08,974
Do you feel that?

97
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:11,520
We get it, you love the ground.

98
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:13,855
Yeah, it's my everywhere friend!

99
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,397
But this is different.

100
00:05:15,398 --> 00:05:16,274
Hmm...

101
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:17,651
I don't feel anything.

102
00:05:17,776 --> 00:05:19,610
A rare sect of earthbenders

103
00:05:19,611 --> 00:05:21,737
can sense things underground.

104
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:23,823
What do you feel?

105
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:27,244
There's something powerful...

106
00:05:27,953 --> 00:05:28,829
below us.

107
00:05:30,997 --> 00:05:32,207
You ready?

108
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:34,834
Wait. Wha...

109
00:05:34,835 --> 00:05:35,836
Wait, wait, wait!

110
00:05:37,963 --> 00:05:40,215
Uh... Okay, what's worse:

111
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:42,633
Leaving the Avatars underground

112
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:45,095
or following
the Avatars underground?

113
00:05:45,804 --> 00:05:48,431
Karthik's gonna bury me
underground.

114
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:51,351
Wait up!

115
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:57,857
And here I thought I knew
every boulder and pebble

116
00:05:57,858 --> 00:05:58,942
in Ellora.

117
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:05,490
I don't think
anyone's been down here

118
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:07,658
for a very long time.

119
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:10,871
Wrong. The Anomaly's been here.

120
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:20,964
- This is creepy.
- What is this place?

121
00:06:21,089 --> 00:06:22,924
I don't know,
but it's gotta be

122
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:24,050
from the Old World.

123
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,051
What's it doing below Ellora?

124
00:06:26,052 --> 00:06:29,972
I'm not scared.
Nope, not one bit.

125
00:06:29,973 --> 00:06:32,808
You felt all of this
with your toes?!

126
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:34,435
I guess I don't know
my own strength?

127
00:06:38,732 --> 00:06:41,025
- Oh, hi!
- They can't see you.

128
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:42,359
It's only polite!

129
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,362
Whoa, an Old World "mover"!

130
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:48,408
The Old World
looks so strange.

131
00:06:52,037 --> 00:06:54,915
We've got to tell Karthik
about this place!

132
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:57,125
Huge discovery
of Old World tech.

133
00:06:57,250 --> 00:07:00,461
Oh, is that Form 17-4 or 17-8?

134
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:05,467
Avatar Korra?

135
00:07:05,926 --> 00:07:07,844
She doesn't look scary.

136
00:07:10,013 --> 00:07:11,348
Did you see that?!

137
00:07:11,473 --> 00:07:13,642
What does Avatar Korra
have to do with this place?

138
00:07:13,767 --> 00:07:16,269
Come back and just tell us
what to do! Come on!

139
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:18,354
Oh! More crystals!

140
00:07:20,649 --> 00:07:22,066
Field trip over!

141
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:24,485
Let's head up
to some lovely singing bowls,

142
00:07:24,486 --> 00:07:26,654
a nice quiet meditation,

143
00:07:26,655 --> 00:07:28,197
and...

144
00:07:28,198 --> 00:07:30,116
...and you've both
run off again.

145
00:07:30,241 --> 00:07:31,451
Great.

146
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,211
Pavi, look at this!

147
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:46,299
Ooh. Look at those arms.

148
00:07:49,344 --> 00:07:50,553
Hey.

149
00:07:50,679 --> 00:07:52,180
That's Aang!

150
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:54,307
And there's Kyoshi,

151
00:07:54,432 --> 00:07:56,476
and I think that's Kuruk.

152
00:07:57,435 --> 00:07:59,770
The world used
to love the Avatars.

153
00:07:59,771 --> 00:08:02,356
How did she go from being adored

154
00:08:02,357 --> 00:08:04,401
to destroying humanity?

155
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:08,196
Huh?

156
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:12,241
Shockingly, this looks
up to code.

157
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:13,659
Okay.

158
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,912
New phobia unlocked!

159
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,372
Get this off me!

160
00:08:21,918 --> 00:08:23,837
Do you hear that?

161
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:27,298
Sharing helmets
is very unhygienic!

162
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:30,927
Pavi?

163
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:35,264
Pavi?

164
00:08:35,265 --> 00:08:36,474
Nisha?

165
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,768
We-we don't want to get lost
down here!

166
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:43,231
I don't want
to get lost down here.

167
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,068
Who's there?!

168
00:09:08,631 --> 00:09:09,673
Uki?!

169
00:09:18,558 --> 00:09:20,184
What are you doing here?

170
00:09:20,185 --> 00:09:21,977
Long story, small kids.
I'll tell you later.

171
00:09:21,978 --> 00:09:23,855
Come on, let's get you back home
where you belong.

172
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:26,356
Jae, you really
shouldn't be here.

173
00:09:26,357 --> 00:09:29,485
Neither should you,
so we're busting you out!

174
00:09:29,486 --> 00:09:31,779
We'll fight off all the Faceless
if we have to!

175
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:35,325
Oh, you sweet airhead.
That's not what I meant.

176
00:09:35,450 --> 00:09:37,159
I <i>want</i> to be here.

177
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,661
What are you talking about?

178
00:09:38,787 --> 00:09:41,539
You've been
bandit-brainwashed!

179
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:46,044
Jae, I didn't want you
to find out like this.

180
00:09:48,088 --> 00:09:49,589
I wasn't taken.

181
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:51,215
I'm with the Faceless.

182
00:10:13,321 --> 00:10:16,157
Remember how we snuck
into the pantry with Daemin?

183
00:10:32,507 --> 00:10:35,260
If you're so scared,
just wait here!

184
00:10:56,030 --> 00:10:57,323
Found you!

185
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:08,417
Please, show me Mom and Dad.

186
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,840
Huh?

187
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,634
What just happened?

188
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:20,638
Where am I?

189
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:23,141
<i>When</i> am I?

190
00:11:26,686 --> 00:11:28,313
Avatar Korra?

191
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:37,238
Whoa!

192
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:44,078
Pavi!

193
00:11:53,338 --> 00:11:55,423
Nisha! Where did Korra go?

194
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,466
You saw Avatar Korra?!

195
00:11:57,467 --> 00:11:59,509
Wait! Pavi!
You can't just go off--

196
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:07,768
Korra?

197
00:12:25,328 --> 00:12:26,663
Is this...

198
00:12:26,788 --> 00:12:28,414
The Cataclysm?

199
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:31,751
That wasn't just Korra's memory.

200
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,168
It's ours.

201
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:36,631
We're connected to her
because we <i>are</i> her.

202
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:38,465
So everything she did...

203
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:41,094
Was her choice. Not ours.

204
00:12:41,219 --> 00:12:44,264
We're nothing like her, right?

205
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:08,412
What were you thinking?

206
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:11,249
We <i>barely</i> survived
the Anomaly last time,

207
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:13,835
and you just jump in
without me?!

208
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:16,838
I can't lose you too!

209
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:19,048
I just...

210
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:21,718
wanted to see Mom and Dad
so badly.

211
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:25,054
Hmm?

212
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:26,514
Jae?

213
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:37,191
So you just left your friends,

214
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:40,278
your family,
without saying goodbye?

215
00:13:40,403 --> 00:13:43,990
How could I tell you,
or anyone?

216
00:13:44,574 --> 00:13:47,284
I'd be a pariah,
and so would my family.

217
00:13:47,285 --> 00:13:50,455
That's why the Faceless
set up a fake kidnapping for me.

218
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,415
So now you pillage? Raid?

219
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:56,376
Sleep in an unsanitary
environment?

220
00:13:56,377 --> 00:13:57,544
Why?!

221
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:59,297
I want freedom.

222
00:13:59,422 --> 00:14:02,174
I never had a choice
in joining the Brigade.

223
00:14:02,175 --> 00:14:04,510
But it's an honor
to serve Ellora!

224
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:06,721
Ever since I was a kid,

225
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:09,766
I've wanted to be a farmer
or a camodillo herder.

226
00:14:10,308 --> 00:14:13,227
I love animals,
and making things grow.

227
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:16,564
Then when I was ten,
I lit my dad's chair on fire.

228
00:14:17,065 --> 00:14:19,400
And all those choices
were ripped away.

229
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:24,072
From then on, I was a bender
for the Brigade, nothing else.

230
00:14:24,197 --> 00:14:25,697
That's not true.

231
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:27,075
Being in the Brigade,

232
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,117
you get to be a part
of something more

233
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,619
than just yourself.

234
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,996
I've always wanted to help.

235
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:36,041
We're not all like you, Jae.

236
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:37,585
Some of us are just...

237
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:38,961
human.

238
00:14:42,590 --> 00:14:44,801
And some people
are just thieves.

239
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:48,178
If you met the Faceless Queen,
you'd understand!

240
00:14:48,179 --> 00:14:50,347
You're coming home with me.

241
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:53,976
Just go, get out of here!

242
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:56,145
Not without you!

243
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:10,201
Are you okay?

244
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:12,870
Oh! Uki?

245
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:14,538
Your pops misses you.

246
00:15:14,539 --> 00:15:16,873
You-you met my family?

247
00:15:16,874 --> 00:15:19,000
He's grumpy, but funny.

248
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:20,586
I promised him I'd find you.

249
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:22,295
We searched everywhere,

250
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:24,048
but you were out
stealing camodillos

251
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:25,674
with your new squad!

252
00:15:25,675 --> 00:15:27,426
Your squad of crime!

253
00:15:27,427 --> 00:15:28,469
Crime?

254
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:32,682
We take what we need,
no more, no less.

255
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:47,155
Easy, Kosal!

256
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,405
They aren't a threat!

257
00:15:48,406 --> 00:15:49,782
The Faceless Queen...

258
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:52,577
You three again.

259
00:15:52,702 --> 00:15:54,327
Interesting.

260
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:55,872
Let the girls go.

261
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,541
Children serving
in the Brigade now?

262
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:02,294
What will Ellora force
its benders to do next?

263
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:04,004
At least we Ellorans
have a sense

264
00:16:04,005 --> 00:16:05,298
of duty and honor.

265
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:09,719
We live free from your
bureaucracy and narrow views.

266
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:11,720
But you hurt people.

267
00:16:15,433 --> 00:16:17,058
The world isn't
as black and white

268
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:19,061
as you've been taught,
little one.

269
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:25,109
Ah, a mother's set.

270
00:16:26,277 --> 00:16:29,154
Mothers have one piece
made for themselves,

271
00:16:29,155 --> 00:16:30,572
the other for their daughter.

272
00:16:30,573 --> 00:16:32,616
So they're always together...

273
00:16:34,035 --> 00:16:35,328
...even far apart.

274
00:16:35,453 --> 00:16:37,830
What's that?

275
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:40,582
That's the sigil
of the artist who made it;

276
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:41,959
a unique signature.

277
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:43,544
How do you know that?

278
00:16:43,669 --> 00:16:45,045
I've separated

279
00:16:45,046 --> 00:16:47,840
many brooches
from their bracelets.

280
00:16:48,424 --> 00:16:50,592
No!

281
00:16:50,593 --> 00:16:53,303
Bring her back! Hey! No! Stop!

282
00:16:55,806 --> 00:16:58,683
The girls?
They can be reeducated.

283
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:00,937
But you?
You're a Brigade bootlicker

284
00:17:01,062 --> 00:17:03,188
through and through.

285
00:17:04,147 --> 00:17:05,316
You can't leave

286
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:07,107
knowing our hideout.

287
00:17:12,615 --> 00:17:14,491
- What is going on?
- What's happening?

288
00:17:20,998 --> 00:17:23,041
The spirit demon is real?!

289
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,171
Get back, everyone!

290
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:29,549
Run!

291
00:17:52,113 --> 00:17:54,240
Uki, don't make me do this.

292
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:01,289
Come with me!

293
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:08,670
Look, there's another tunnel.

294
00:18:08,671 --> 00:18:11,424
They won't find you, trust me.

295
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:17,346
Tell my grandpa
you kept your promise

296
00:18:17,471 --> 00:18:18,513
and that I'm okay.

297
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:20,056
Oh, wait!

298
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:22,017
Please tell me you know
this song!

299
00:18:26,689 --> 00:18:28,940
Oh yeah.
That's called "Return to Me."

300
00:18:28,941 --> 00:18:31,568
People sing it all the time
in the Eastern Outskirts.

301
00:18:31,569 --> 00:18:33,070
Thank you, Uki!

302
00:18:33,195 --> 00:18:35,238
I forgive you
for your bandit ways!

303
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:36,032
I don't.

304
00:18:37,575 --> 00:18:39,327
You can still come home.

305
00:18:40,077 --> 00:18:42,455
You know what I've always
admired about you, Jae?

306
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:46,458
You're a big softie
who loves protecting people.

307
00:18:46,459 --> 00:18:48,544
You belong in the Brigade.

308
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:49,754
I don't.

309
00:18:51,172 --> 00:18:52,506
Don't try to find me again.

310
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:01,349
And don't bring kids

311
00:19:01,474 --> 00:19:03,851
to an underground bandit lair,
you goof!

312
00:19:14,654 --> 00:19:17,823
You're not going anywhere!

313
00:19:42,098 --> 00:19:45,685
Huh, scrappy girl's full
of surprises.

314
00:19:46,102 --> 00:19:48,978
Ha! The Faceless Queen!

315
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:50,563
This is huge!

316
00:19:50,564 --> 00:19:53,191
In the name of Ellora,
I arrest you.

317
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:57,071
Oh. I'm shaking in my boots.

318
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:00,866
Huh?

319
00:20:11,669 --> 00:20:12,794
Jae!

320
00:20:12,795 --> 00:20:14,505
Remember when you chased me here

321
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:16,589
and I saved your butt?

322
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,341
We were so young back then.

323
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:19,719
Let's get home.

324
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:32,564
So everything they said
about her was true.

325
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:37,737
Pavi, what we saw...

326
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:40,530
You were right
about the Anomaly.

327
00:20:40,531 --> 00:20:44,410
If it's connected to Korra,
I want nothing to do with it.

328
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:49,122
Good, time to put
this Anomaly stuff behind us.

329
00:20:49,123 --> 00:20:51,082
Let's make that Fortress of Mud!

330
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,585
Ooh, or we could steal
Hamka's fake mustache.

331
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:56,337
We don't need to get zapped

332
00:20:56,338 --> 00:20:58,298
now that we've got this sigil!

333
00:20:58,299 --> 00:21:00,426
Uki even narrowed down
our search:

334
00:21:00,551 --> 00:21:02,469
the Eastern Outskirts!

335
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:05,306
We barely escaped the Faceless
<i>and</i> the Anomaly,

336
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:08,391
and you wanna risk putting us
in danger again?!

337
00:21:08,392 --> 00:21:11,103
Don't you want to know
what happened to Mom and Dad?

338
00:21:11,854 --> 00:21:13,898
I have to do this.

339
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:37,045
I'm shocked you historians
of New Ba Sing Se

340
00:21:37,046 --> 00:21:39,799
left your crumbling haven
to join this party.

341
00:21:39,924 --> 00:21:41,549
And a gearhead brat

342
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:44,344
like yourself can be
from nowhere but Akasha.

343
00:21:44,345 --> 00:21:47,055
What are you looking for?
Adult supervision?

344
00:21:47,056 --> 00:21:50,351
What can I say?
Curiosity's got the best of me.

345
00:21:50,935 --> 00:21:54,271
Whatever made Kayoko send out
the call, it's gotta be big.

